From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:59:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/gud: avoid compile-time fortify trap on TV mode names

With clang ThinLTO and -O3, linking gud.o fails:

  ld.lld: error: call to __read_overflow marked "dontcall-error":
  detected read beyond size of object (1st parameter)

gud_connector_add_tv_mode() kmallocs buf_len =
GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_MAX_NUM * GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN bytes and
then checks each of the ret / GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN names for a
NUL with a fortified memchr(). usb_control_msg() never returns more
than the requested length, but that is not visible at this call site.
At -O3 the loop gets unrolled and peeled, and the compiler emits a
memchr() at a constant offset past the kmalloc() size. FORTIFY_SOURCE
turns that into a hard link error.

Two changes:

  - reject a reply longer than the buffer, which makes the bound
    explicit (it also keeps modes[] from being indexed past MAX_NUM)
    and is a no-op for any real device. This alone is enough for
    clang 22, but not for clang 21 (Fedora 43) or clang 23
    (openSUSE Tumbleweed), which still emit the peeled call.
  - test for the terminator with strnlen() instead of memchr(). The
    two are equivalent here: a name is valid iff a NUL occurs within
    GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN bytes. The fortified strnlen() only
    checks at run time, so a path the optimizer cannot rule out no
    longer becomes a link error.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
@@ -390,7 +390,7 @@
 			  connector->index, buf, buf_len);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto free;
-	if (!ret || ret % GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN) {
+	if (!ret || ret > buf_len || ret % GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN) {
 		ret = -EIO;
 		goto free;
 	}
@@ -399,7 +399,7 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < num_modes; i++) {
 		char *mode = &buf[i * GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN];
 
-		if (!memchr(mode, '\0', GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN)) {
+		if (strnlen(mode, GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN) == GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN) {
 			ret = -EIO;
 			goto free;
 		}
